course: dictionary
lesson: 12332
title: Brave words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Courageous is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a courageous person, a courageous act. It means brave. «The firefighter was courageous when she ran into the smoke to save the cat.» Running into smoke is dangerous, so courageous must mean brave in a frightening place.
explain: Courage does not always mean fighting. «It was courageous of Sam to tell the teacher the truth, even though he was scared.» The clue is scared: Sam felt afraid but did the right thing anyway. What word would fit there? Brave would fit, so courageous means brave.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «It was brave of Sam to tell the teacher the truth» still makes sense, so you have understood the word correctly.
fact: Courageous means brave: willing to do something frightening, difficult or dangerous because it is right.
fact: Courageous is an adjective. Its other forms are more courageous and most courageous.
fact: «A courageous act» is one brave deed, and «a courageous decision» is a brave choice.
fact: Courage can mean saying no, telling the truth or helping someone being bullied, not only fighting.
fact: Being courageous means acting even though you feel afraid.
exercise: «The courageous rescuer climbed into the icy river to pull out the boy.» What does courageous mean here? | Lost and confused | Cold and wet | *Brave, willing to face danger for someone else | Very quick at swimming
exercise: Which word could replace courageous in «a courageous decision»? | sleepy | silly | *brave | lazy
exercise: Yusuf says courageous means the same as frightened. Is he right? | Yes, both words mean scared and worried | No, courageous means funny | Yes, because both words are used in dangerous places | *No, courageous means brave, so it describes someone who is willing to face fear
test: «It was courageous of Mia to admit she had broken the window.» What does this sentence show about Mia? | *She was brave and honest, even though it was hard | She was asleep at the time | She was lost and confused | She was careless and did not care
test: Which word is a synonym for courageous? | *brave | lazy | quiet | fearful
exam: Which example shows the most courage? | Hid under the table during the fight | *Stood up for a classmate who was being bullied, even though he was scared | Stayed silent when a classmate was being bullied | Ran away when a friend was in trouble
